preConditionHook:
// EEC E24's MoneyFlow(length), the `moneyflow` register row (VERIFIED,
// EL_MoneyFlow_Probe.txt, 0/9,821 bars at 4.3e-10):
//   MF = 100 * pos / (pos + neg) over `length` current-inclusive bars;
//   money flow per bar = typical price (H+L+C)/3 x TICKS -- the TOTAL
//   up+down tick count (ctx.Ticks), NOT the up-tick `volume` alias
//   (EL_Volume_Probe.txt); a bar adds to pos when its TP is above the
//   previous bar's, and to neg OTHERWISE (ties share the else branch);
//   sums are fresh, newest-first; and there is NO clamp -- with negative
//   back-adjusted prices the ratio legitimately leaves 0..100 (598.8
//   measured on @OJ Aug 2008), so do not "fix" values outside the range.
// TP is a pure price function, so every lag reads real chart history.
// The TP comparison is toleranced (el_gt): TP is a computed value, and
// EL-source functions carry the relational tolerance internally; the
// probe's fit cannot distinguish raw from toleranced here (both matched),
// so this follows the corpus convention for EL-source internals.
double mfPos = 0.0;
double mfNeg = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)length; ++i) {
    double tpNow = (high[i] + low[i] + close[i]) / 3;
    double tpPrev = (high[i + 1] + low[i + 1] + close[i + 1]) / 3;
    double flow = tpNow * (double)ctx.Ticks[i];
    if (el_gt(tpNow, tpPrev)) { mfPos += flow; }
    else { mfNeg += flow; }
}
// pos + neg == 0 needs every bar's TP x Ticks to sum to exactly zero --
// unreachable on real data (the probe had 0 such bars); EL would divide
// by zero and raise (the zero-denominator register row), and this mirror
// does not guard either.
mfVal = 100.0 * mfPos / (mfPos + mfNeg);
// EL `crosses` is a STATE MACHINE (the `crosses above/below` register
// row, VERIFIED): fires when the toleranced comparison holds AND the most
// recent NON-equal bar was on the other side; equality runs are bridged;
// the side starts UNKNOWN (0), so nothing fires on the first evaluated
// bar. One independent state per threshold line.
crossUpOversold = el_gt(mfVal, oversold) && lastSideOversold == -1;
crossDownOverbought = el_lt(mfVal, overbought) && lastSideOverbought == 1;
if (el_gt(mfVal, oversold)) { lastSideOversold = 1; }
else if (el_lt(mfVal, oversold)) { lastSideOversold = -1; }
if (el_gt(mfVal, overbought)) { lastSideOverbought = 1; }
else if (el_lt(mfVal, overbought)) { lastSideOverbought = -1; }
